    "hero.btn2": "Test Your Knowledge",
    "hero.stat1": "Earth covered by water",
    "hero.stat2": "Warming limit",
    "hero.stat3": "People on Earth",
    "hero.scroll": "Scroll to explore",

    "s1.tag": "Slide 01",
    "s1.title": "Our Planet, Our Home",
    "s1.lead": "Earth is the only known planet that can support life. Its air, water, soil and climate work together in a delicate balance that keeps every living thing alive.",
    "s1.c1t": "Right Conditions for Life",
    "s1.c1p": "Earth has oxygen, liquid water, and a temperature range that allows plants, animals, and humans to survive. No other known planet has this.",
    "s1.c2t": "Nature Supports Us",
    "s1.c2p": "Forests clean the air, rivers carry fresh water, bees pollinate crops, and soil grows our food. Nature is the system that keeps us alive.",
    "s1.c3t": "A Balance to Protect",
    "s1.c3p": "When one part of nature is damaged — forests, oceans, air, or soil — the effects spread. Environmental balance keeps our home healthy.",
    "s1.quote": "“Earth is not just where we live. It is our home, our life, and our future.”",

    "s2.tag": "Slide 02",
    "s2.title": "What Does Nature Give Us?",
    "s2.lead": "Everything we need to live comes from nature. These gifts are free, but they are not unlimited — they must be used wisely.",
    "s2.a1t": "Fresh Air", "s2.a1p": "Plants and trees release the oxygen we breathe and filter dust.",
    "s2.a2t": "Clean Water", "s2.a2p": "Rivers, lakes, and rainfall supply the fresh water we drink and use.",
    "s2.a3t": "Food", "s2.a3p": "Healthy soil, sunlight, and water allow farmers to produce our food.",
    "s2.a4t": "Forests", "s2.a4p": "Forests cool the land, hold soil in place, and shelter wildlife.",
    "s2.a5t": "Resources", "s2.a5p": "Wood, minerals, and metals come from the Earth. Use them carefully.",
    "s2.a6t": "Medicines", "s2.a6p": "Many modern medicines are based on compounds found in plants.",
    "s2.a7t": "Habitats", "s2.a7p": "Forests, wetlands, and oceans are homes for millions of species.",
    "s2.a8t": "Beauty", "s2.a8p": "Mountains, beaches, and green spaces bring us joy and calm.",

    "s3.tag": "Slide 03",
    "s3.title": "The Importance of Trees",
    "s3.lead": "Trees are the lungs of our planet. A single mature tree can absorb around 22 kilograms of carbon dioxide each year.",
    "s3.c1t": "They Produce Oxygen",
    "s3.c1p": "Through photosynthesis, trees take in carbon dioxide and release oxygen. Without trees, the air we breathe would not exist.",
    "s3.c2t": "They Absorb CO₂",
    "s3.c2p": "Forests store carbon in their wood and roots. This slows global warming and keeps the climate stable.",
    "s3.c3t": "They Protect Wildlife",
    "s3.c3p": "Forests are homes for birds, insects, and countless other species. When forests disappear, animals lose their shelter.",
    "s3.c4t": "They Help Rainfall",
    "s3.c4p": "Trees release water vapour into the air, helping form clouds and rain. They also prevent soil erosion.",
    "s3.calloutT": "Why Deforestation Is Dangerous",
    "s3.calloutP": "Cutting down forests destroys habitats, increases CO₂, causes soil erosion and flooding, and reduces rainfall. Forests that took centuries to grow can be lost in days.",

